      justification: "libpdx-argv.M4-001 + ENH-013 (Closes #23) case31 — `-vv` on COUNTED flag `v`. Register `v\\0` as FKIND_BOOL id=100 (the COUNTED idiom is BOOL + count_flag_by_id at the read side; no dedicated FKIND_COUNTED exists in libpdx-argv's kind space). Parser expands `-vv` into two independent stores, flag_count reaches 2, and count_flag_by_id(100) returns 2 — the same result `-v -v` would produce. Regression witness for the mainstream repeat-count idiom now working inside a cluster. Non-leaf: 1-push (rbx) aligns rsp%16 for the nested full_reset / flag_spec_register / parse_argv / count_flag_by_id / find_flag_by_id / record_* calls.",
      block: {
